bjects; it cannot establish a reproducible difference between cultures.</p><h3 class="reading-heading--topic">Open every field directly</h3><ul><li>blank (no transfect): <a href="https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6460/wiki/aerosense-assets-20261017/5e630e6fdce2-field-01-panel.webp">Field 1</a>, <a href="https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6460/wiki/aerosense-assets-20261017/ade17f66130a-field-02-panel.webp">Field 2</a>, <a href="https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6460/wiki/aerosense-assets-20261017/b75a71323ade-field-03-panel.webp">Field 3</a></li><li>ORCO only: <a href="https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6460/wiki/aerosense-assets-20261017/543a1b4d8437-field-01-panel.webp">Field 1</a>, <a href="https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6460/wiki/aerosense-assets-20261017/5b0eda8645d6-field-02-panel.webp">Field 2</a>, <a href="https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6460/wiki/aerosense-assets-20261017/9f65790930c9-field-03-panel.webp">Field 3</a></li><li>Or7a+ORCO: <a href="https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6460/wiki/aerosense-assets-20261017/6ec5ffe3634a-field-01-panel.webp">Field 1</a>, <a href="https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6460/wiki/aerosense-assets-20261017/8a33d3bf11bc-field-02-panel.webp">Field 2</a></li><li>Or19a+ORCO: <a href="https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6460/wiki/aerosense-assets-20261017/7643929086f7-field-01-panel.webp">Field 1</a>, <a href="https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6460/wiki/aerosense-assets-20261017/1088e1fabeff-field-02-panel.webp">Field 2</a></li><li>Or22a+ORCO: <a href="https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6460/wiki/aerosense-assets-20261017/ff50a0484725-field-01-panel.webp">Field 1</a>, <a href="https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6460/wiki/aerosense-assets-20261017/dfc6de291134-field-02-panel.webp">Field 2</a></li><li>Or35a+ORCO: <a href="https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6460/wiki/aerosense-assets-20261017/6ffc966fa86b-field-01-panel.webp">Field 1</a>, <a href="https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6460/wiki/aerosense-assets-20261017/0aa3e5249242-field-02-panel.webp">Field 2</a></li><li>Or42a+ORCO: <a href="https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6460/wiki/aerosense-assets-20261017/9b8cd373d02c-field-01-panel.webp">Field 1</a>, <a href="https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6460/wiki/aerosense-assets-20261017/58dc99b58155-field-02-panel.webp">Field 2</a></li><li>Or59b+ORCO: <a href="https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6460/wiki/aerosense-assets-20261017/d4968628a670-field-01-panel.webp">Field 1</a>, <a href="https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6460/wiki/aerosense-assets-20261017/897883fcf383-field-02-panel.webp">Field 2</a></li><li>Or67a+ORCO: <a href="https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6460/wiki/aerosense-assets-20261017/da1f071b719e-field-01-panel.webp">Field 1</a>, <a href="https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6460/wiki/aerosense-assets-20261017/70ce46e447ea-field-02-panel.webp">Field 2</a></li><li>Or67b+ORCO: <a href="https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6460/wiki/aerosense-assets-20261017/38ddc265d08b-field-01-panel.webp">Field 1</a>, <a href="https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6460/wiki/aerosense-assets-20261017/01479bfc7ecf-field-02-panel.webp">Field 2</a></li><li>Or85b+ORCO: <a href="https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6460/wiki/aerosense-assets-20261017/e6d56c8fe0fc-field-01-panel.webp">Field 1</a></li><li>Or98a+ORCO: <a href="https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6460/wiki/aerosense-assets-20261017/f47134a04c4c-field-01-panel.webp">Field 1</a>, <a href="https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6460/wiki/aerosense-assets-20261017/22348c24a9de-field-02-panel.webp">Field 2</a></li></ul><p>We excluded ambiguous connected regions instead of forcing a cell count through the dense aggregates. The <a href="#table-object-fractions">condition table</a> gives the number of positive objects and the denominator explicitly. “DAPI foreground retained” is the eligible objects’ share of segmented blue area, <strong>not the fraction of all cells or nuclei retained</strong>. The low retained area warns that these estimates sample the easier-to-segment portion of each field.</p><h3 class="reading-heading--topic">Density and thresholds matter</h3>
 <p>The images contain broad connected DAPI regions and clipping at the maximum exported value. Even a sharp edge around a fluorescent patch can contain several overlapping nuclei. Retaining a small, isolated subset avoids inventing divisions within those clusters, but introduces a selection bias. The excluded regions remain visible in every overlay.</p>
 <p>Threshold choice also matters. For Or98a + Orco, the RED-positive fraction changes from 30.8% at the less stringent blank P95 threshold to 0.7% at P99. We use the conservative P99 rule as the primary analysis and report the full sensitivity table.</p>
